  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f53a79b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Raw UART link + one-shot capture\n",
    "\n",
    "`mspm0l2228_aes_trigger.c` speaks a raw protocol (`'p'`+16 bytes → `'r'`+16\n",
    "bytes), so we drive the serial line directly rather than via SimpleSerial.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Wiring (verified firmware labels):** MSPM0 `UART0` is **PA10 = TX**, **PA11 =\n",
    "RX** at **115200 8N1**; the trigger `GPIO_TRIG` is **PA0** (package pin 1), idle\n",
    "low. Connect **PA10 → Husky tio1** (scope `serial_rx`), **Husky tio2 → PA11**\n",
    "(scope `serial_tx`), **PA0 → Husky tio4**, and a common **GND**. The Husky does\n",
    "**not** drive the MSPM0 clock (async capture)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "23dda1f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "def _to_bytes(s):\n",
    "    return bytes(bytearray(map(ord, s))) if isinstance(s, str) else bytes(s)\n",
    "\n",
    "def capture_one(pt16, timeout=200):\n",
    "    target.flush()\n",
    "    scope.arm()\n",
    "    target.write(b'p' + bytes(pt16))\n",
    "    if scope.capture():                 # True == timeout (no trigger)\n",
    "        return None, None\n",
    "    wave = scope.get_last_trace()\n",
    "    resp = _to_bytes(target.read(17, timeout=timeout))\n",
    "    if len(resp) < 17 or resp[0:1] != b'r':\n",
    "        return wave, None               # trace captured but framing off\n",
    "    return wave, resp[1:17]             # (wave, ciphertext)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a9a0bc5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Sanity check: one trace\n",
    "\n",
    "Confirm the link and that the trigger window holds the AES burst. Retune `scope.gain.db` if the trace is clipped (flat) or tiny."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "99106ebf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "ciphertext: 8c9e4121b5134c0edda4e65207a1d229\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x300 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng()\n",
    "pt = rng.integers(0, 256, 16, dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "wave, ct = capture_one(pt)\n",
    "assert wave is not None, 'No trigger — check GPIO_TRIG -> tio4 wiring and firmware.'\n",
    "print('ciphertext:', ct.hex() if ct else 'NO/!=r framing — check BAUD and protocol')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12,3))\n",
    "plt.plot(wave, linewidth=0.6)\n",
    "plt.title('MSPM0 AES-ADV power trace (one ECB block)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Sample'); plt.ylabel('Power'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "efee9d01-2fc1-4d22-8254-4075ef99cbbc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "link OK   ciphertext: 1a985c4cb6a90564d6b2ae2bb416e139\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Optional: UART link test ONLY (no scope / no trigger needed).\n",
    "# Verifies the 'p' -> 'r' protocol independently of the GPIO_TRIG wiring, so you\n",
    "# can tell a serial problem apart from a trigger problem.\n",
    "import time\n",
    "target.flush(); time.sleep(0.1); target.flush()      # clear any stale bytes\n",
    "\n",
    "pt = bytes(16)                                        # all-zero plaintext\n",
    "target.write(b'p' + pt)                               # raw bytes, matches firmware\n",
    "time.sleep(0.05)\n",
    "resp = _to_bytes(target.read(17, timeout=300))\n",
    "if len(resp) == 17 and resp[0:1] == b'r':\n",
    "    print('link OK   ciphertext:', resp[1:17].hex())\n",
    "    # AES128-ECB(2b7e...4f3c, 0^16) == 7df76b0c1ab899b33e42f047b91b546f\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'link FAIL  got {len(resp)} byte(s):', resp.hex())\n",
    "    print('  -> check BAUD=115200, PA10(TX)->tio1, tio2->PA11(RX), common GND')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "116a6e26",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Capture the attack set\n",
    "\n",
    "Random plaintexts; record the **ciphertext** per trace (the last-round attack needs ciphertexts). Saved to `mspm0_hwaes_traces.npz`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "32ea6748",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "ef5dcf1b5b8f4c5b96d14975bf1a9a0e",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "Capturing:   0%|          | 0/100000 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "kept 100000, dropped 0; 2000 samples each; saved to npz (~800 MB in RAM)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from tqdm.notebook import trange\n",
    "\n",
    "# Preallocated + interruptible. Also saves plaintexts (textins) so the recovered key\n",
    "# can be verified blindly (re-encrypt a known pt, compare to its ct), and so a\n",
    "# first-round attack is possible. Ctrl-C keeps what was captured.\n",
    "traces   = np.empty((N_TRACES, SAMPLES), dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "textouts = np.empty((N_TRACES, 16),      dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "textins  = np.empty((N_TRACES, 16),      dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "n = bad = 0\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    for _ in trange(N_TRACES, desc='Capturing'):\n",
    "        pt = rng.integers(0, 256, 16, dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "        w, ct = capture_one(pt)\n",
    "        if w is None or ct is None:\n",
    "            bad += 1; continue\n",
    "        traces[n]   = w\n",
    "        textins[n]  = pt\n",
    "        textouts[n] = np.frombuffer(ct, dtype=np.uint8)   # ct is bytes -> uint8 row\n",
    "        n += 1\n",
    "except KeyboardInterrupt:\n",
    "    print(f'interrupted — keeping the {n} traces captured so far')\n",
    "\n",
    "traces   = traces[:n]; textouts = textouts[:n]; textins = textins[:n]\n",
    "save = dict(traces=traces, textouts=textouts, textins=textins)\n",
    "if KNOWN_KEY is not None:\n",
    "    save['key'] = np.frombuffer(KNOWN_KEY, dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "np.savez('mspm0_hwaes_traces.npz', **save)\n",
    "print(f'kept {n}, dropped {bad}; {traces.shape[1]} samples each; saved to npz '\n",
    "      f'(~{traces.nbytes/1e6:.0f} MB in RAM)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2642d3ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5b. Signal-quality gate — are we measuring the chip at all?\n",
    "\n",
    "Before any attack, confirm MEASURE actually sees the MSPM0's current. Averaging\n",
    "all traces cancels random noise, so a real capture leaves a clear AES **burst**;\n",
    "a dead-flat averaged trace means the shunt / power path isn't carrying the chip's\n",
    "current (turning up gain won't help). Fix that before running §6b / §7."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "d9dba538",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "ADC range used       : 0.293 of ~1.0   (raise scope.gain.db if below ~0.2)\n",
      "averaged-trace std   : 0.005353\n",
      "expected noise floor : 0.000009\n",
      "VERDICT: signal present — proceed\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x260 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# 5b. Signal-quality gate — did we actually MEASURE the chip's current?\n",
    "# A valid capture (a) fills a fair bit of the ADC range and (b) has a deterministic\n",
    "# AES 'burst' that survives averaging. A flat averaged trace means the MEASURE input\n",
    "# isn't seeing the chip (shunt / power-path problem) — no attack can work until fixed.\n",
    "_rng   = float(traces.max() - traces.min())                 # vs ~1.0 full scale\n",
    "_m     = traces.mean(0)                                     # averaged trace\n",
    "_sig   = _m.std()\n",
    "_noise = (traces.std(0) / np.sqrt(len(traces))).mean()      # expected noise in the mean\n",
    "print(f'ADC range used       : {_rng:.3f} of ~1.0   (raise scope.gain.db if below ~0.2)')\n",
    "print(f'averaged-trace std   : {_sig:.6f}')\n",
    "print(f'expected noise floor : {_noise:.6f}')\n",
    "print('VERDICT:', 'signal present — proceed' if _sig > 3*_noise else\n",
    "      'NO CHIP SIGNAL — fix the shunt / power path, re-capture (do not attack yet)')\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12,2.6)); plt.plot(_m, lw=0.6)\n",
    "plt.title('Averaged trace — should show the AES burst'); plt.xlabel('Sample')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "386fd497-4e02-4019-a773-289405320a35",
