    "## 7b. Profile the leak points (one-time, uses a known-key device)\n",
    "\n",
    "Template-attack model: on a device whose key you control, find **where** each key byte\n",
    "leaks and in which direction. The result (points-of-interest + weights) is saved to\n",
    "`mspm0_poi_profile.npz` and reused to attack an **unknown** key in 7c — the POI *locations*\n",
    "are a property of the hardware, not the key. **This is the only step that uses a known key.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "61110117",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Profiling (needs a known-key capture): per-byte points-of-interest + leak-direction\n",
    "# weights. Saved to disk; 7c/8 then recover a key WITHOUT ever reading it.\n",
    "assert KNOWN_KEY is not None, 'Profiling needs a known-key capture (7c/8 then run key-free).'\n",
    "M_POI = 3\n",
    "_td = traces - traces.mean(0); _tss = np.sqrt((_td**2).sum(0)) + 1e-12\n",
    "poi_idx = np.zeros((16, M_POI), int); poi_w = np.zeros((16, M_POI))\n",
    "for b in range(16):\n",
    "    c   = textouts[:, b].astype(np.uint8)\n",
    "    mt  = HW[INV_SBOX[(c ^ K10_true[b]).astype(np.uint8)]]; mtc = mt - mt.mean()\n",
    "    loc = (_td.T @ mtc) / (_tss * (np.sqrt((mtc**2).sum()) + 1e-12))\n",
    "    p = np.argsort(np.abs(loc))[::-1][:M_POI]\n",
    "    poi_idx[b] = p; poi_w[b] = loc[p]\n",
    "np.savez('mspm0_poi_profile.npz', poi_idx=poi_idx, poi_w=poi_w)\n",
    "print(f'profiled {M_POI} POIs/byte; saved mspm0_poi_profile.npz')\n",
    "print('strongest leak sample per byte:', poi_idx[:, 0].tolist())\n",
    "print('-> 7c/8 recover the key using ONLY these POIs + ciphertexts (no key).')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md7cattack",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7c. Attack — recover the key (the key is NOT used here)\n",
    "\n",
    "Loads the saved profile and recovers each round-10 key byte by correlating the\n",
    "matched-filtered POI projection with `HW(InvSbox(C_b⊕k))` over all 256 guesses. Nothing in\n",
    "this cell or 8 reads the key: set `KNOWN_KEY=None` (and skip 6b/7b, reusing a saved\n",
    "`mspm0_poi_profile.npz` from a known-key device) and it still runs. 8 verifies the result\n",
    "blindly by AES-re-encrypting a stored plaintext."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "code7cattack",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
